% ============================================================
\chapter{Abstract}
% ============================================================

The Smart Personal Finance \& Goal Management System is a web-based application designed to help users manage income, expenses, budgets and financial goals in one place. The system combines transaction management with rule-based financial intelligence, anomaly detection, forecasting and scenario simulation.

The proposed system follows a modular architecture with a React/Tailwind frontend, a REST API backend using Java and a MySQL database. The analytics layer uses transaction history to identify spending patterns, recurring behaviour and unusual transactions. A rule engine converts financial conditions into understandable alerts and recommendations, while Monte Carlo simulation is used for goal and scenario projections.

The main objective is to provide users with a clear dashboard, structured financial records and explainable insights that can support better personal financial planning.

% ============================================================
\chapter{Introduction and Problem Statement}
% ============================================================

Managing personal finances often involves multiple disconnected activities such as recording transactions, checking account balances, setting budgets, tracking savings goals and evaluating future financial plans. A user may therefore have the data but still lack a simple way to understand spending behaviour and the effect of different financial decisions.

The proposed Smart Personal Finance \& Goal Management System addresses this problem by combining core personal-finance management with automated analysis. The system provides a single interface for transactions, categories, budgets and goals and extends these features with behaviour analysis, anomaly detection, a rule engine, forecasting and scenario comparison.

\section{Problem Statement}

Users need a simple and structured system to:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item record and categorize income and expenses;
    \item monitor balances and spending patterns;
    \item create and track budgets;
    \item create financial goals and monitor their progress;
    \item identify unusual spending behaviour;
    \item understand the reasons behind financial alerts;
    \item compare possible financial scenarios; and
    \item receive understandable recommendations based on their financial data.
\end{itemize}

\section{Objectives}

The main objectives are:
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
    \item Develop secure user registration and login using JWT authentication.
    \item Provide transaction creation, viewing, updating, deletion and categorization.
    \item Provide budget creation and monitoring.
    \item Provide financial goal creation and progress tracking.
    \item Generate monthly, category-wise and trend-based spending summaries.
    \item Detect unusual or anomalous spending behaviour.
    \item Implement a configurable rule engine for financial alerts.
    \item Implement forecasting and Monte Carlo based scenario simulation.
    \item Compare financial scenarios and generate explainable recommendations.
    \item Provide a clean dashboard for balances, spending, goals and insights.
    \item Test the application using unit, integration and property-based testing.
\end{enumerate}

