\chapter{Testing Strategy}
% ============================================================

Testing is planned at multiple levels:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{Unit testing:} individual backend functions, rules and calculations.
    \item \textbf{Integration testing:} interaction between frontend, backend and database.
    \item \textbf{Property-based testing:} validation of financial rules and calculations using Hypothesis.
    \item \textbf{Authentication testing:} login, protected routes and user-access control.
    \item \textbf{API testing:} validation of request and response behaviour.
    \item \textbf{Regression testing:} repeated verification after feature integration.
    \item \textbf{CI testing:} automated checks through GitHub Actions.
\end{itemize}

% ============================================================
\chapter{Expected Outcome}
% ============================================================

The expected outcome is a working web application that combines personal-finance record keeping with financial intelligence. A user should be able to record transactions, monitor budgets and goals, inspect spending patterns, receive alerts about unusual behaviour and compare possible financial scenarios through a single dashboard.

The system is also designed to keep recommendations understandable by connecting them to financial conditions and configurable rules rather than presenting unexplained outputs.

% ============================================================
\chapter{Conclusion}
% ============================================================

The Smart Personal Finance \& Goal Management System integrates personal financial management, analytics and decision-support features into one application. The proposed architecture separates the frontend, backend, database and intelligence components, allowing the team to develop and test the system in parallel.

The project begins with a focused MVP and then extends it with anomaly detection, rule-based insights, forecasting, Monte Carlo simulation and scenario comparison. The combination of these modules is intended to provide a structured and explainable approach to personal financial planning.

